ect.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":58281,"output_tokens":2185,"requests":4}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify whether the mid-redeploy defer shares the existing DEFER_FILE/DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX episode with the inflight>0 busy-defer path or uses a distinct episode key, and define the reset/continuation semantics when a tick transitions between busy and mid-redeploy dispositions, so the bound genuinely cannot live-lock.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'DEFER (retry next tick) with a countable AUTODEPLOY_DEFERRED bot-redeploying marker, bounded by the existing DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX episode'","Code: DEFER_FILE is a single shared state file; the inflight>0 branch writes/reads defer_since from it (lines 813-833) and clears it on deploy (line 850, 1160)","ABSENCE: the plan does not state whether the redeploying-disposition defer writes the SAME DEFER_FILE as the busy defer, so it is unclear whether a busy-then-redeploy sequence resets the timer (never bounding) or shares it (one disposition prematurely exhausting the other's bound)"],"finding":"Fix 3 reuses the existing single DEFER_FILE / DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX episode (shared with the inflight>0 busy-defer path) but does not specify whether the mid-redeploy defer shares that same timer/file or uses a distinct episode key, leaving the interaction between a busy episode and a redeploy episode ambiguous.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa05a997281994ec8","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Fix 3 (\"bounded by the existing DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX episode\"); infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh DEFER_FILE lines 73, 813-833, 850, 1160","norm_id":"na13025b903531a98","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A bot is busy (inflight>0) for several ticks accumulating a defer episode, then becomes briefly unreachable mid-redeploy — does the redeploy defer continue the same episode timer or start fresh?","Alternating busy and mid-redeploy ticks could reset defer_since each time, defeating the DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX bound the plan claims to preserve"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["5 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Specify that the `draining`-flag check and the gauge increment in the certified-op wrapper share a single atomic critical section with `begin_draining()` (lock/CAS, no check-then-act TOCTOU), and add a test that a request racing begin_draining() is deterministically either fully counted-and-drained or refused.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.884,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'add a `draining` flag to `InFlightGauge` (`begin_draining()`), and have the certified-op wrapper REFUSE a new certified op ... once draining'","Plan: '_on_sigterm calls begin_draining() FIRST' — sigterm handler and request handlers run concurrently; the plan does not state whether the flag-read + gauge-increment is a single atomic critical section (lock/CAS) shared with begin_draining()"],"finding":"Fix 1 adds a new `draining` flag to `InFlightGauge` and gates the certified-op wrapper on it (check draining, then increment), but the plan never specifies the atomicity of that check-then-act against concurrent certified requests arriving while `_on_sigterm` calls `begin_draining()`. A request that reads `draining==False` and then increments the gauge after `begin_draining()` runs (TOCTOU) would slip a new op into the gauge during drain, defeating the 'burst cannot re-pin the port' invariant.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7a01d77bc16bf391","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Fix 1 (`draining` flag / begin_draining / certified-op wrapper REFUSE)","norm_id":"n3a1ed81153be58d6","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A certified request handler evaluates `draining` as False, is preempted, `_on_sigterm` sets draining and reads gauge==0, then the preempted handler increments — the fast-drain-at-0 window ships a live op the drain loop no longer waits on, or the port is re-pinned exactly as the fix intends to prevent."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"State that `begin_draining()`, the `draining` read, and the increment execute under the same gauge lock (or CAS), so no request can observe `draining==False` and then increment after drain has begun; assert this in the gauge-level test.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State a concrete default value (seconds) for DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS in the plan, so the executor need not choose the backstop duration.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5022,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["'Add a short constant DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS for uvicorn.Config(timeout_graceful_shutdown=...)'","AC only asserts 'timeout_graceful_shutdown == DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS < DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS' — no absolute value","This is a defaultable threshold gap (signals 1/2): the backstop duration is asserted-by-name but never given a number"],"finding":"The new constant DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS is introduced as 'a short constant' but no concrete value is stated; the executor must choose it, and the only stated bound is '< 1200s'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3f77ea3823b609ea","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Fix 1; Acceptance Criteria line 1","norm_id":"n7c69a2af68ad8d04","priority":0.2978,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor picks an arbitrarily short (e.g. 1s) or long value; if too short, a slow idle-stream sweep could be truncated in edge cases; if too long, the deploy_errors symptom partially recurs"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Name a specific value (e.g. DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS = 30) with a one-line rationale that it comfortably exceeds a normal idle-stream sweep while staying far below the 1200s op grace.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"324b5b2d9218f720","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["8dc037